{%- doc -%}
  Repeats, in <head>, the theme stylesheets that sections link from inside
  the page body.

  Sections load their own CSS with <link rel="stylesheet"> next to their
  markup. Chrome waits for those files before painting, Safari does not:
  it paints the content with only the head CSS and restyles it a moment
  later (oversized images, unstyled layout for a split second). Shopify
  renders sections before the layout, so their HTML is available here;
  every theme stylesheet found in it is linked once in <head>, where all
  browsers wait for it. The body links stay for the theme editor and
  Section Rendering API responses; the browser reuses the same file.

  @param {string} html - Rendered HTML to scan (the first template sections, a captured section group).
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign kt_css_parts = html | split: 'rel="stylesheet" href="'
  assign kt_css_seen = ''
  for part in kt_css_parts offset: 1
    assign kt_css_href = part | split: '"' | first
    if kt_css_href contains '/assets/' and kt_css_href contains '.css'
      unless kt_css_seen contains kt_css_href
        assign kt_css_seen = kt_css_seen | append: kt_css_href | append: ' '
        echo '<link rel="stylesheet" href="' | append: kt_css_href | append: '" media="all">'
      endunless
    endif
  endfor
-%}
